$termsBody = <<<'PCTERMS'
        <p>These terms set out how PowerCabs Ireland Limited (&ldquo;PowerCabs&rdquo;) handles airport transfers, designated pickup locations, waiting times, Meet &amp; Greet services and no-shows. They apply in addition to the Customer Terms and to the cancellation policy applicable to the service booked.</p>
        <p>Company: PowerCabs Ireland Limited<br>Customer support: admin@powercabs.ie<br>Website: https://powercabs.ie</p>

        <h2 id="a-1" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">1. Booking Time and Customer Responsibilities</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">1.1 Confirmed booking time</h3>
        <p>The pickup time provided by the customer and confirmed by PowerCabs is the scheduled time at which the passenger is expected to be ready to meet the assigned driver at the designated pickup location, subject to any flight-monitoring or revised-pickup arrangement expressly applicable to the booking.</p>
        <p>PowerCabs recognises that airport formalities, including immigration, visa checks, baggage collection and other airport procedures, may cause delays. Nevertheless, customers are responsible for selecting a suitable pickup time, allowing sufficient time for these procedures and reaching the designated meeting point within the applicable waiting period.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">1.2 Customer communication</h3>
        <p>Customers must provide accurate contact details and remain reasonably contactable around the scheduled pickup time. If a passenger anticipates a delay, they should notify PowerCabs or the assigned driver as soon as reasonably practicable.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">1.3 Waiting periods</h3>
        <p>The applicable waiting period depends on the service booked:</p>
        <ul class="tw-mb-4 tw-ml-5 tw-flex tw-list-disc tw-flex-col tw-gap-1.5">
          <li>Standard airport pickup, including Standard Meet &amp; Greet: maximum 20 minutes from the confirmed pickup time.</li>
          <li>Meet &amp; Assist: maximum 30 minutes from the confirmed pickup time.</li>
          <li>First Class Meet &amp; Greet: maximum 45 minutes from the original confirmed booking time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These periods are maximum pickup/no-show windows, not a guarantee of unlimited waiting or a commitment to extend the booking because a passenger is delayed.</p>
        <p>The 10-minute grace period for standard airport pickups is included within the applicable 20-minute maximum; it is not an additional 10 minutes on top of that maximum.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">1.4 No-show</h3>
        <p>Where the applicable maximum waiting period has expired, the passenger has not appeared at the designated meeting point, and reasonable attempts to resolve the situation have been unsuccessful where practicable, the driver may report the booking as a no-show.</p>
        <p>PowerCabs will assess the applicable charge or refund under the disclosed booking terms and applicable law. A no-show report does not, by itself, determine the customer&rsquo;s legal entitlement to a refund.</p>

        <h2 id="a-2" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">2. Standard Airport Pickup and Waiting Charges</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">2.1 Ten-minute grace period</h3>
        <p>For standard airport pickups, including Standard Meet &amp; Greet, PowerCabs allows a 10-minute grace period from the confirmed pickup time for the passenger to meet the driver.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">2.2 Additional waiting time</h3>
        <p>If the passenger has not arrived within the first 10 minutes, the driver may report the delay to PowerCabs. Additional waiting charges may apply where they have been disclosed to the customer before booking and are permitted under the applicable terms.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">2.3 Maximum waiting period</h3>
        <p>The maximum waiting period for a standard airport pickup, including Standard Meet &amp; Greet, is 20 minutes from the confirmed pickup time.</p>
        <p>For example, if the confirmed pickup time is 11:00, the passenger is expected to meet the driver by 11:10. Additional waiting charges may apply after 11:10. If the passenger has not appeared by 11:20, the booking may be treated as a no-show.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">2.4 No-show charges and refunds</h3>
        <p>Where a passenger fails to appear within the applicable waiting period and the driver has attended the agreed pickup location as required, PowerCabs may apply the applicable disclosed no-show charge.</p>
        <p>PowerCabs may charge an authorised waiting-time or cancellation amount to the payment method used for the booking, subject to the customer&rsquo;s payment authorisation, the disclosed terms and applicable law.</p>
        <p>Any decision to retain the full fare or decline a refund will be subject to the applicable contract, the circumstances of the booking and mandatory consumer protection rights. The maximum waiting period does not automatically authorise a charge that would otherwise be unlawful.</p>

        <h2 id="a-3" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">3. Premium Airport Pickups and Flight Monitoring</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">3.1 Flight monitoring</h3>
        <p>Where flight monitoring is included in the booked Premium or First Class service, PowerCabs will use reasonably available flight information to monitor the relevant flight and adjust the driver&rsquo;s dispatch or arrival arrangements where practicable.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">3.2 Changes to flight arrival times</h3>
        <p>Where the airline updates the expected arrival time, PowerCabs may adjust the driver&rsquo;s dispatch in accordance with the updated information. Flight monitoring is intended to reduce unnecessary waiting and improve coordination; it does not guarantee that every delay or change will be detected or accommodated.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">3.3 Applicable waiting period</h3>
        <p>Flight monitoring and passenger waiting time are separate matters. The maximum waiting period is determined by the service booked:</p>
        <ul class="tw-mb-4 tw-ml-5 tw-flex tw-list-disc tw-flex-col tw-gap-1.5">
          <li>Standard airport pickup or Standard Meet &amp; Greet: 20 minutes.</li>
          <li>Meet &amp; Assist: 30 minutes.</li>
          <li>First Class Meet &amp; Greet: 45 minutes.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>A Premium booking does not automatically qualify for the 45-minute First Class waiting period unless that period is expressly included in the confirmed service.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">3.4 First Class Meet &amp; Greet &mdash; 45-minute maximum</h3>
        <p>For First Class Meet &amp; Greet, the maximum no-show period is 45 minutes from the original confirmed booking time. A flight delay or revised flight arrival time does not automatically restart this 45-minute period.</p>
        <p>For example, if the original confirmed booking time is 11:00, the flight is initially delayed until 11:20 and is subsequently delayed by a further 20 minutes, the 45-minute maximum still runs from 11:00. The passenger must therefore meet the driver by 11:45 unless PowerCabs expressly confirms a revised arrangement.</p>
        <p>The 45-minute period is not calculated from 11:15 or from the end of a separate 15-minute grace period.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">3.5 Passenger notification</h3>
        <p>Customers should notify PowerCabs promptly if flight information changes, they cannot locate the driver, or they expect to exceed the applicable waiting period. Any additional waiting or revised arrangement remains subject to confirmation and availability.</p>

        <h2 id="a-4" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">4. Meet &amp; Assist</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">4.1 Waiting period</h3>
        <p>Meet &amp; Assist bookings have a maximum waiting period of 30 minutes from the applicable confirmed pickup time, unless a different arrangement is expressly confirmed by PowerCabs.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">4.2 Assistance included</h3>
        <p>Where Meet &amp; Assist has been selected and confirmed, the driver will provide reasonable assistance within the scope of the service booked, which may include helping the passenger with their luggage and accompanying or assisting them towards the agreed meeting point, where operationally practicable.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">4.3 Limits of assistance</h3>
        <p>The service does not automatically include specialist mobility assistance, medical care, wheelchair provision, porter services or assistance requiring airport authorisation unless expressly confirmed in advance.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">4.4 Delays</h3>
        <p>If the passenger has not appeared within the 30-minute maximum, the driver may report a no-show. Any applicable charge or refund will be determined under the disclosed booking terms and applicable law.</p>

        <h2 id="a-5" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">5. Airport Pickup and Drop-Off Locations</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">5.1 Airport drop-offs</h3>
        <p>For airport drop-off journeys, customers who have not booked Meet &amp; Greet will be dropped off at the designated terminal drop-off area applicable to their flight and vehicle access arrangements.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">5.2 Standard airport pickup &mdash; Dublin Airport</h3>
        <p>For standard airport pickup bookings without Meet &amp; Greet, the designated meeting point is Zone 18 at Dublin Airport, subject to airport rules, access restrictions and any updated instructions provided by PowerCabs.</p>
        <p>Customers should follow the pickup instructions in their booking confirmation and contact PowerCabs if they cannot locate the designated area.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">5.3 Meet &amp; Greet &mdash; Terminal 1</h3>
        <p>For Meet &amp; Greet bookings at Terminal 1, the designated meeting point is the arrivals hall beside Insomnia Coffee.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">5.4 Meet &amp; Greet &mdash; Terminal 2</h3>
        <p>For Meet &amp; Greet bookings at Terminal 2, the designated meeting point is the arrivals hall beside the yellow sculpture.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">5.5 Changes to airport access or meeting points</h3>
        <p>Airport layouts, access rules and designated pickup locations may change. If airport authorities impose restrictions or PowerCabs must change the meeting point for operational or safety reasons, PowerCabs will endeavour to notify the customer and provide updated instructions as soon as reasonably practicable.</p>
        <p>The customer is responsible for following the latest confirmed pickup instructions.</p>

        <h2 id="a-6" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">6. Luggage and Additional Assistance</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">6.1 Advance disclosure</h3>
        <p>Customers must provide accurate information about the number, size and nature of their luggage when booking, particularly where they require Meet &amp; Greet or Meet &amp; Assist services.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">6.2 Oversized or excessive luggage</h3>
        <p>Any oversized, unusually heavy or excessive luggage, or any luggage requiring special handling, must be disclosed and agreed with PowerCabs in advance.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">6.3 Service limitations</h3>
        <p>If the customer arrives with luggage that was not disclosed and that cannot safely or reasonably be accommodated, the driver may refuse the additional luggage or the affected service where necessary for safety, vehicle capacity or operational reasons.</p>
        <p>Where the customer has failed to disclose material luggage requirements and the booked service cannot reasonably be provided as a result, any cancellation charge or refund will be assessed under the applicable booking terms and law. No automatic forfeiture of the entire fare applies where it would be unlawful.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">6.4 Customer responsibility</h3>
        <p>Customers must ensure that the selected vehicle and service are suitable for their passengers and luggage. Where in doubt, customers should contact PowerCabs before confirming the booking.</p>

        <h2 id="a-7" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">7. Driver and Customer Conduct, Contact Details and Off-Platform Arrangements</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">7.1 Respectful communication</h3>
        <p>PowerCabs expects professional, respectful and courteous communication between drivers and customers at all times. Abusive, threatening, discriminatory or harassing conduct will not be tolerated.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">7.2 Personal contact information</h3>
        <p>Drivers and customers should use the communication channels provided or authorised by PowerCabs for booking-related matters. They should avoid sharing personal telephone numbers or other private contact details unless there is a legitimate reason and they have freely agreed to do so.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">7.3 Off-platform arrangements</h3>
        <p>Bookings made through PowerCabs should be managed through PowerCabs&rsquo; authorised booking and payment systems. Neither a driver nor a customer should represent a private arrangement as a PowerCabs booking unless PowerCabs has expressly authorised it.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">7.4 Responsibility for unauthorised arrangements</h3>
        <p>Where a driver and customer independently exchange personal contact details and arrange subsequent journeys or services outside PowerCabs&rsquo; systems without PowerCabs&rsquo; knowledge or authorisation, PowerCabs may be unable to monitor, administer or provide customer support for those private arrangements.</p>
        <p>To the extent permitted by law, PowerCabs is not responsible for the performance of an independent arrangement that it neither authorised nor controlled. However, this clause does not exclude or limit any liability, duty of care or statutory right that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">7.5 Reporting concerns</h3>
        <p>Customers and drivers may report inappropriate conduct, unauthorised use of PowerCabs&rsquo; name or disputes relating to a PowerCabs booking through the appropriate company support channels.</p>

        <h2 id="a-8" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">8. Incorrect or Incomplete Flight Information</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">8.1 Customer responsibility</h3>
        <p>The customer or booking representative is responsible for providing accurate flight details, including the airline, flight number, arrival date and scheduled arrival time where requested.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">8.2 Corrections</h3>
        <p>Any error or change must be reported to PowerCabs as soon as reasonably practicable. PowerCabs may attempt to verify the supplied details or contact the booking representative where clarification is required.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">8.3 Incorrect flight details</h3>
        <p>Where incorrect or incomplete flight information prevents PowerCabs from identifying or monitoring the correct flight, the pickup arrangement may be affected. PowerCabs cannot guarantee that it will identify every error, particularly where the customer does not respond to a clarification request.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">8.4 Refund assessment</h3>
        <p>Where no driver has been assigned, PowerCabs may offer a 50% refund of the amount paid for the affected booking, with any retained amount subject to the disclosed terms, fairness, proportionality and applicable law.</p>
        <p>Where a driver has already been assigned and attended the designated airport pickup area in accordance with the confirmed booking, PowerCabs may apply the applicable disclosed no-show or cancellation charge if the passenger cannot be located within the relevant waiting period.</p>
        <p>The assignment or attendance of a driver does not, by itself, remove any statutory entitlement to a refund.</p>

        <h2 id="a-9" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">9. Evidence, Complaints and Refund Reviews</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">9.1 Operational records</h3>
        <p>PowerCabs may use relevant records to review disputes, including dispatch timestamps, available location information, communication records, flight details and driver reports.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">9.2 Requests for evidence</h3>
        <p>Customers may request a review of driver attendance or a no-show decision by emailing admin@powercabs.ie and providing their booking reference, travel date and details of the issue.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">9.3 Fair review</h3>
        <p>PowerCabs will review complaints fairly and in good faith, taking account of the available evidence, the terms disclosed at booking and applicable law.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">9.4 Privacy</h3>
        <p>Any evidence shared with customers will be subject to applicable data protection and privacy requirements. PowerCabs will not disclose unnecessary personal information about drivers or other passengers.</p>

        <h2 id="a-10" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">10. Waiting-Time Payments, Cancellation Charges and Driver Settlement</h2>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">10.1 Authorised payment method</h3>
        <p>Where the customer has been informed of the applicable charge and has authorised payment, PowerCabs may charge the payment method used for the booking for applicable waiting-time charges or cancellation/no-show charges.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">10.2 Charge transparency</h3>
        <p>The amount or method of calculating any waiting-time or no-show charge must be disclosed clearly before the booking is confirmed. Charges must be fair, proportionate and permitted by applicable law.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">10.3 Driver settlement</h3>
        <p>Where a cancellation or no-show charge is validly retained, PowerCabs may allocate an amount to the assigned driver in accordance with the applicable driver agreement and commission arrangements.</p>
        <p>The driver&rsquo;s agreed payment will be calculated under that agreement, less PowerCabs&rsquo; commission where applicable.</p>

        <h3 class="tw-mb-2 tw-mt-6 tw-text-lg tw-font-bold tw-text-ink">10.4 No effect on customer rights</h3>
        <p>The internal allocation of money between PowerCabs and a driver does not increase the customer&rsquo;s liability or determine the customer&rsquo;s entitlement to a refund. Any amount retained from the customer must be independently justified under the booking terms and applicable law.</p>

        <h2 id="a-11" class="tw-mb-3 tw-mt-10 tw-text-2xl tw-font-bold">11. General Legal Provisions</h2>
        <p>11.1. These terms must be read alongside the relevant booking confirmation, general PowerCabs terms and conditions, and the cancellation policy applicable to the service.</p>
        <p>11.2. Nothing in these terms excludes or limits any consumer right, remedy or liability that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited under Irish or applicable EU law.</p>
        <p>11.3. PowerCabs will retain relevant booking and operational records for an appropriate period, subject to applicable data protection and record-retention requirements.</p>
        <p>11.4. If any provision is found to be unenforceable, the remaining provisions will continue to apply to the extent permitted by law.</p>
        <p>11.5. These terms are governed by the laws of Ireland, subject to any mandatory consumer protection laws applicable to the customer.</p>
        <p>PowerCabs Ireland Limited<br>Service with Excellence</p>
